    "items": [
      {
        "id": "lem-tdmath-euler-identity-for-degree-one-homogeneous-function",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Euler identity for a differentiable degree-one homogeneous function",
        "statement": "Let $C\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be open and $f:C\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^1$. Suppose that for every $x\\in C$ there is a nondegenerate interval $J_x\\subset(0,\\infty)$ containing $1$ such that $\\lambda x\\in C$ and $f(\\lambda x)=\\lambda f(x)$ for every $\\lambda\\in J_x$. Here nondegenerate means that $J_x$ contains a point different from $1$; $1$ may be an endpoint. Then\n\n$$f(x)=Df(x)[x]=\\sum_{j=1}^d x_j\\,\\partial_j f(x)\\qquad(x\\in C).$$\n\nThe radial identity need only hold on one side of $1$: openness of $C$ and $C^1$ regularity supply an ambient derivative, and the interval makes $1$ a nonisolated point at which that derivative is determined by the radial identity. This uses the same function on the same domain; it asserts nothing about a family of functions on different tagged domains.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Daniel Arovas, Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics, §2.7",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Book:_Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics_(Arovas)/02:_Thermodynamics/2.07:_Thermodynamic_Potentials"
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "inventory_expansion_required": true,
        "library": "physics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-tdmath-smooth-partial-legendre-transform-differential",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Differential of a smooth partial Legendre transform on a local inverse chart",
        "statement": "Let $\\mathcal O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^k\\times\\mathbb R^m$ be open with $k,m\\ge1$, and let $f:\\mathcal O\\to\\mathbb R$ be $C^2$. Suppose the map $(u,z)\\mapsto(x,z):=(D_u f(u,z),z)$ restricts to a $C^1$ diffeomorphism between open neighborhoods, with inverse $(x,z)\\mapsto(g(x,z),z)$. Define\n\n$$\\widehat f(x,z):=f(g(x,z),z)-x\\cdot g(x,z).$$\n\nThen $\\widehat f$ is $C^2$ and\n\n$$d\\widehat f=-g\\cdot dx+D_z f(g(x,z),z)\\cdot dz.$$\n\nThis is a local statement. Existence of the inverse chart is a hypothesis; the lemma asserts no global inverse or boundary transform.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "thm-chain-sum-product-and-composition-rules-for-banach-derivatives",
          "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-chain-sum-product-and-composition-rules-for-banach-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Daniel Arovas, Thermodynamics and Statistical Mechanics, Appendix II, §2.15",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Book:_Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics_(Arovas)/02:_Thermodynamics/2.15:_Appendix_II-_Legendre_Transformations"
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "inventory_expansion_required": true,
        "library": "physics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "def-td-legendre-potentials",
        "kind": "definition",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Local thermodynamic Legendre potentials",
        "statement": "Fix a material constitution $c$ with finite species list $(1,\\ldots,r)$ and a local energy representation $U_c=U_c(s,V,n_1,\\ldots,n_r)$ from [[pthm-td-local-energy-representation]]. Here $s$ is entropy in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, $V>0$ is volume in $\\mathrm{m^3}$, each $n_j>0$ is in $\\mathrm{mol}$, $U_c$ is in joules, and the conjugates are $T=U_{c,s}$ in kelvins, $p=-U_{c,V}$ in pascals, and $\\mu_j=U_{c,n_j}$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}}$. The derivatives hold every other listed natural coordinate fixed; the physical-coordinate and rest-frame conventions are those of [[def-td-equilibrium-state-domain]] and [[def-td-si-quantities]].\n\nFor an open chart, a **local Legendre transformation** means the following partial transformation of $U_c$: select one or more of its extensive coordinates $q$, take their conjugate coordinates $x=D_qU_c$, and use only a neighborhood on which $(q,z)\\mapsto(x,z)$, with $z$ the untransformed coordinates, has a $C^1$ inverse. Such a neighborhood is a valid local transform chart in the sense of [[def-td-response-functions]]. No inverse or potential as a function of the proposed natural coordinates is asserted outside that chart.\n\nOn their respective valid charts define the enthalpy, Helmholtz potential, Gibbs potential, and grand potential by\n\n$$H_c:=U_c+pV,\\qquad F_c:=U_c-Ts,\\qquad G_c:=U_c-Ts+pV,\\qquad \\Omega_c:=U_c-Ts-\\sum_{j=1}^r\\mu_jn_j.$$\n\nTheir natural-coordinate charts are respectively $(s,p,n)$, $(T,V,n)$, $(T,p,n)$, and $(T,V,\\mu_1,\\ldots,\\mu_r)$. In the volume transform the conjugate coordinate is $-p=U_{c,V}$, which accounts for the plus sign in $H_c$ and $G_c$; in the chemical transform the conjugates are $\\mu_j=U_{c,n_j}$, which accounts for the minus signs in $\\Omega_c$. All four potentials have units of joules. A displayed differential or global convex-duality characterization is not part of this definition; critical, coexistence, and other non-C2 boundaries are excluded.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
          "def-td-si-quantities",
          "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
          "def-td-response-functions",
          "pthm-td-local-energy-representation"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-response-functions": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "pthm-td-local-energy-representation": "physical-result"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
