            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "physical_scope": "Local C2 single-phase thermodynamic charts in the adopted nonrelativistic SI framework; transformed natural-variable charts are used only where the specified coordinate maps have C1 inverses.",
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-potential-differentials",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Differentials of the thermodynamic potentials",
        "statement": "On a valid local energy-representation chart from [[pthm-td-local-energy-representation]], let $s,V,n_j,U,T,p,\\mu_j$ and the potentials $H,F,G,\\Omega$ be as defined in [[def-td-legendre-potentials]]. On every open neighborhood where the corresponding natural-coordinate maps have their stated $C^1$ inverses, the potentials are C2 and their differentials are\n\n$$dU=T\\,ds-p\\,dV+\\sum_{j=1}^r\\mu_j\\,dn_j,\\qquad dH=T\\,ds+V\\,dp+\\sum_{j=1}^r\\mu_j\\,dn_j,$$\n\n$$dF=-s\\,dT-p\\,dV+\\sum_{j=1}^r\\mu_j\\,dn_j,\\qquad dG=-s\\,dT+V\\,dp+\\sum_{j=1}^r\\mu_j\\,dn_j,$$\n\n$$d\\Omega=-s\\,dT-p\\,dV-\\sum_{j=1}^r n_j\\,d\\mu_j.$$\n\nAll differentials are local state-function differentials. They do not assert that heat or work is an exact differential on process space.",
        "deps": [
          "pthm-td-local-energy-representation",
          "def-td-legendre-potentials",
          "lem-tdmath-smooth-partial-legendre-transform-differential"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "pthm-td-local-energy-representation": "physical-result",
          "def-td-legendre-potentials": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-tdmath-smooth-partial-legendre-transform-differential": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
