              "title": "Jeremy Tatum, Heat and Thermodynamics, §17.6, The Gibbs-Duhem Relation",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Heat_and_Thermodynamics_(Tatum)/17:_Chemical_Thermodynamics/17.06:_The_Gibbs-Duhem_Relation"
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 9,
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "physical_scope": "Conditional local identities on a positive-temperature C2 energy-representation chart when the same fixed material tag satisfies degree-one homogeneity on that chart; the separately designated common-bulk constitutive-law branch supplies this condition through its entropy transport on local inverse charts with common species, intensive parameters, units and energy/entropy references. The general tagged-scaling postulate alone does not provide it.",
        "library": "physics",
        "proof_strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-maxwell-relations",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Maxwell relations on valid thermodynamic potential charts",
        "statement": "Let $U,H,F,G,\\Omega$ and their natural-coordinate charts be as in [[def-td-legendre-potentials]], with the exact differentials supplied by [[pthm-td-potential-differentials]]. Assume each potential is C2 on its named open chart. Every pair of conjugate coefficients in its exact differential has equal cross derivatives. Explicitly, with all unlisted natural coordinates held fixed, for each species $i,j$:\n\n- From $U(s,V,n)$: $T_V|_{s,n}=-p_s|_{V,n}$; $T_{n_j}|_{s,V,n}=\\mu_{j,s}|_{V,n}$; $-p_{n_j}|_{s,V,n}=\\mu_{j,V}|_{s,n}$; and $\\mu_{i,n_j}|_{s,V}=\\mu_{j,n_i}|_{s,V}$.\n- From $H(s,p,n)$: $T_p|_{s,n}=V_s|_{p,n}$; $T_{n_j}|_{s,p,n}=\\mu_{j,s}|_{p,n}$; $V_{n_j}|_{s,p,n}=\\mu_{j,p}|_{s,n}$; and $\\mu_{i,n_j}|_{s,p}=\\mu_{j,n_i}|_{s,p}$.\n- From $F(T,V,n)$: $s_V|_{T,n}=p_T|_{V,n}$; $s_{n_j}|_{T,V,n}=-\\mu_{j,T}|_{V,n}$; $-p_{n_j}|_{T,V,n}=\\mu_{j,V}|_{T,n}$; and $\\mu_{i,n_j}|_{T,V}=\\mu_{j,n_i}|_{T,V}$.\n- From $G(T,p,n)$: $-s_p|_{T,n}=V_T|_{p,n}$; $-s_{n_j}|_{T,p,n}=\\mu_{j,T}|_{p,n}$; $V_{n_j}|_{T,p,n}=\\mu_{j,p}|_{T,n}$; and $\\mu_{i,n_j}|_{T,p}=\\mu_{j,n_i}|_{T,p}$.\n- From $\\Omega(T,V,\\mu)$: $s_V|_{T,\\mu}=p_T|_{V,\\mu}$; $s_{\\mu_j}|_{T,V,\\mu_{k\\ne j}}=n_{j,T}|_{V,\\mu}$; $p_{\\mu_j}|_{T,V,\\mu_{k\\ne j}}=n_{j,V}|_{T,\\mu}$; and $n_{i,\\mu_j}|_{T,V,\\mu_{k\\ne j}}=n_{j,\\mu_i}|_{T,V,\\mu_{k\\ne i}}$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-legendre-potentials",
          "pthm-td-potential-differentials",
          "thm-clairaut-schwarz-mixed-partials"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-legendre-potentials": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "pthm-td-potential-differentials": "physical-result",
          "thm-clairaut-schwarz-mixed-partials": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
