      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-useful-work-bound",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Useful-work bound from the Gibbs potential",
        "statement": "For a fixed-composition closed system coupled to an ideal thermal reservoir at $T_0>0$ and ideal pressure store at $p_0>0$, let $Q$ be heat into the system and let $W_{\\mathrm{out}}$ be net energy delivered by the system to an ideal work store whose entropy is constant. Assume the isolated-composite bookkeeping of [A1]–[A3] in Facts & Assumptions. Then for any admitted process between equilibrium endpoints $x_i,x_f$,\n\n$$W_{\\mathrm{out}}\\le G_{T_0,p_0}(x_i)-G_{T_0,p_0}(x_f),\\qquad G_{T_0,p_0}(x):=U(x)+p_0V(x)-T_0S(x).$$\n\nIf the endpoint states lie on the $(T,p)=(T_0,p_0)$ natural-variable chart, this is the decrease in the Gibbs potential of [[def-td-legendre-potentials]]. Equality requires zero total entropy production; the theorem does not assert that a protocol realizing equality exists.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-legendre-potentials",
          "def-td-process-and-protocol",
          "post-td-first-law-energy",
          "post-td-macroscopic-second-law",
          "def-td-si-quantities"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-legendre-potentials": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-process-and-protocol": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-first-law-energy": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-macroscopic-second-law": "physical-assumption",
          "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
