      {
        "id": "pthm-td-heat-capacity-relation",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Heat-capacity relation on a stable response chart",
        "statement": "On an open C2 Helmholtz chart $F(T,V,n)$ at fixed composition $n$, suppose $T>0$, $V>0$, the response coordinates $(T,p,n)$ have the local inverse required by [[def-td-response-functions]], and $\\kappa_T>0$. Then\n\n$$C_p-C_V=\\frac{TV\\alpha_p^2}{\\kappa_T}.$$\n\nHere $C_V,C_p$ are the whole-system heat capacities, $\\alpha_p=V^{-1}(\\partial V/\\partial T)_{p,n}$, and $\\kappa_T=-V^{-1}(\\partial V/\\partial p)_{T,n}$, all as in [[def-td-response-functions]]. The formula is a conditional model identity, not an empirical law or a claim at singular response points.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-response-functions",
          "pthm-td-potential-differentials",
          "pthm-td-maxwell-relations",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "thm-chain-sum-product-and-composition-rules-for-banach-derivatives"
