        "id": "pthm-td-compressibility-capacity-ratio",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Ratio of isothermal and isentropic compressibilities",
        "statement": "On an open C2 Helmholtz chart at fixed composition $n$, assume $T>0$, $C_V>0$, $\\kappa_T>0$, and valid local response inverses for both the isothermal and isentropic compressibilities. Then $C_p>0$, $\\kappa_S>0$, and\n\n$$\\frac{\\kappa_T}{\\kappa_S}=\\frac{C_p}{C_V}.$$\n\nThe heat capacities are whole-system values; $\\kappa_S$ is defined in [[def-td-isentropic-compressibility]]. The hypotheses exclude zero-capacity and singular-chart limits.",
        "deps": [
