        "id": "ex-td-response-chart-failure",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "A smooth chart with no isothermal pressure inverse",
        "statement": "Fix the amount of substance and stipulate the local entropy representative\n\n$$S(U,V)=C\\ln(U/U_*)+aV+S_0$$\n\non the open domain $U>0$, $V>0$, where $C>0$ has units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, $U_*>0$ has units joules, $a>0$ has units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}\\,m^{-3}}$, and $S_0$ has units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$. This chart is finite, C2, concave, and has $S_U>0$. It illustrates that a smooth positive-temperature chart need not admit pressure as a local coordinate at fixed temperature.\n\nThe displayed entropy is $S^{\\rm SI}$ in physical SI coordinates. For this constructed local model, choose the positive-amount open neighborhood stated here (or any positive neighborhood of the fixed amount, extending this entropy independently of amount) and let $O_c$ be the numerical preimage of that product patch under $\\Phi_c(\\hat U,\\hat V,\\hat n)=(\\hat U\\,\\mathrm J,\\hat V\\,\\mathrm{m^3},\\hat n\\,\\mathrm{mol})$. Declare $O_c$ as the model's local state-domain patch and set $S_c=S^{\\rm SI}\\circ\\Phi_c$. The derivatives below are those of $S^{\\rm SI}=S_c\\circ\\Phi_c^{-1}$ on $\\Phi_c(O_c)$, exactly as in [[def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential]]. This supplies the numerical-to-SI chart identification for the formal witness, with no assertion of a measured material or a global constitutive extension.",
        "deps": [
          "def-td-si-quantities",
          "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
